# Browser safety

## Host URLs

Never put `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` in a URL shown to the user. Resolve
`$HOST` per `global-host-url` for any link you hand them. Loopback is fine for
agent-side curls only.

## Secrets and captures

- Do not screenshot or paste pages that show tokens, passwords, session
  cookies, or private personal data into chat.
- Redact or crop before attaching evidence. Prefer assertion text over full-page
  dumps when that is enough.

## When not to browse

- No explicit GUI / web QA ask → do not open a browser.
- Prefer IDE browser MCP over CLI; refuse a private headless process when a
  ready IDE browser MCP covers the action (`browser-automation`).
- Do not use the browser to bypass a ready MCP for the same product (GitHub,
  Jira, etc.) — `global-mcp-first`.
